\title{Subtree size}
\date{2026-11-25T22:10:30Z}
\tag{algorithms}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{If #{r} is some node in a binary search tree, let #{S(r)} be the \em{size} of the subtree rooted at #{r}, that is, the number of nodes which have #{r} as their ancestor (including #{r} itself).}
